.Sh DESCRIPTION
An
.Vt dtfl_arranged
is the indexed form of a
.Vt dtfl_collection :
a shared, reference-counted trace of
.Pq key , value , time , diff
updates, maintained by one writer and read by many operators on the same
worker.
The cost of indexing a collection is paid once and shared, which is why
join, reduce and count read an arrangement rather than a collection.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_arrange
indexes
.Va c
into a shared trace, exchanging updates by record so each record is
accumulated on one worker, batching every input-frontier interval into a
batch, and committing the batches to a spine.
It indexes the whole record as the key.
.Va name
labels the operator, or is
.Dv NULL
for the default.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arrange_from_upsert
arranges a stream of keyed upserts.
Each record of
.Va upserts
is a key followed by an
.Vt option
value: one tag byte, 0 for None and 1 for Some, then the value when Some.
The update's embedded time is the upsert time, and the diff is ignored.
The collection holds, for each key, the most recent value by time; a None
uninstalls the key.
The operator computes the retractions itself, so the result trace indexes
key to value with signed diffs.
A repeated value produces no change, and a tie in time takes the greatest
.Vt option
value
.Pq None < Some .
The time class must be totally ordered.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arranged_as_collection
reads an arrangement back as a collection.
Each stored
.Pq key , value
becomes zero or more output records of
.Va out_type :
.Va fn
writes them from the key and value bytes through the emit handle with
.Fn dtfl_arranged_emit_record ,
and the operator pairs each with every
.Pq time , diff
of that
.Pq key , value .
When
.Va fn
is
.Dv NULL ,
the output record is the stored record itself and
.Va out_type
must be the collection's record type.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arranged_trace
extracts a shareable trace handle: a new reader of the shared trace that may
outlive the arrangement.
.Fn dtfl_trace_import
brings a trace into another dataflow scope on the same worker, producing a
second arrangement over the same backing data; this is how one index serves
several downstream operators.
A trace is worker-local and imports only into dataflows on the worker that
created it.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arranged_enter
and
.Fn dtfl_arranged_leave
carry an arrangement into a child scope and back, lifting each time with the
scope refinement.
The entered arrangement shares the outer trace: operators that read it see
every time lifted into the child scope, and the compaction holds they set
reach the outer trace mapped back to its times.
A trace taken from an entered arrangement cannot be passed to
.Fn dtfl_trace_import ,
which panics; import the outer trace and enter the result.
.Fn dtfl_arranged_enter_region
and
.Fn dtfl_arranged_leave_region
apply to a region, a subscope with the same time class, where no time
transform is needed.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arranged_type ,
.Fn dtfl_arranged_diff
and
.Fn dtfl_arranged_scope
report the record type, the difference class and the scope the arrangement
belongs to.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arranged_stream
returns the arrangement's batch stream, which carries one opaque record per
sealed batch.
It is owned by the scope.
Attach a probe to it with
.Fn dtfl_stream_probe_with
.Pq see Xr dtfl_probe_new 3
to observe the arrangement's progress without reading its records.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_collection_arrange ,
.Fn dtfl_arrange_from_upsert ,
.Fn dtfl_trace_import ,
and the enter and leave functions return a new
.Vt dtfl_arranged
handle the caller owns.
.Fn dtfl_arranged_as_collection
returns a new collection.
.Fn dtfl_arranged_trace
returns a new trace handle.
.Sh OWNERSHIP
.Fn dtfl_arranged_free
and
.Fn dtfl_trace_free
release a handle.
Freeing a handle releases its compaction hold on the shared trace, which lets
the trace compact further; a handle that is never freed holds compaction at
its frontier for as long as the dataflow runs.
The shared trace lives until its last reader is freed.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Every handle belongs to the worker that created it and must not be used from
another thread.
A trace imports only into dataflows on its own worker.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl-differential 7
.Sh STANDARDS
